// dyn-u64(100) - dyn-u64(58) = 42
// Both operands are dynamic (MLOAD round-trip) and range-proven u64 (AND mask),
// so the SUB range-based u64 fast path applies. No underflow: result limb0 = 42,
// upper limbs zero.
// Push b = 58 first (second from top), then a = 100 (top); SUB computes a - b.
PUSH1 0x3a
PUSH1 0x00
MSTORE
PUSH1 0x00
MLOAD
PUSH8 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
AND
PUSH1 0x64
PUSH1 0x00
MSTORE
PUSH1 0x00
MLOAD
PUSH8 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
AND
SUB
PUSH1 0x00
MSTORE
PUSH1 0x20
PUSH1 0x00
RETURN
